\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Head of Thy church triumphant,
\par We joyfully adore Thee,
\par Till Thou appear,
\par Thy members here
\par Shall sing like those in glory
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par We lift our hearts and voices
\par With blest anticipation,
\par And cry aloud,
\par And give to God
\par The praise of our salvation.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The name we still acknowledge
\par That burst our bonds in sunder,
\par And loudly sing
\par Our conquering King,
\par In songs of joy and wonder.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In every day's deliverance
\par Our Jesus we discover;
\par 'Tis He, 'tis He
\par That smote the sea,
\par And led us safely over!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. While in affliction's furnace,
\par And passing through the fire,
\par Thy love we praise,
\par Which knows our days
\par And ever brings us nigher.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par We clap our hands exulting
\par In Thine almighty favour;
\par The love divine
\par Which made us Thine
\par Shall keep us Thine for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. By faith we see the glory
\par To which Thou shalt restore us;
\par The Cross despise
\par For that high prize
\par Which Thou hast set before us.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And if Thou count us worthy,
\par We each, as dying Stephen,
\par Shall see Thee stand
\par At God's right hand
\par To take us up to heaven.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

